A host interface for driving Previous from scripts

- PREVIOUS_SCC_A_PTY and PREVIOUS_SCC_B_PTY connect the serial ports to
  pseudo terminals, and PREVIOUS_SCC_A_LOG and PREVIOUS_SCC_B_LOG log
  what the NeXT sends on them.
- SIGUSR1 sends a serial break on channel A (the kernel's magic SysRq),
  SIGUSR2 raises an NMI.
- SIGHUP saves the screen shown in the main window as a PNG to
  PREVIOUS_SCREENSHOT, which works while the host's display is locked.
- PREVIOUS_INPUT names a FIFO of keyboard and mouse commands (type, key,
  down, up, move, button), sent one event at a time at typing speed.

next68k-linux's scripts (run-previous.sh, console.py, serial-run.py,
sysrq.sh, nmi.sh, screenshot.sh, input.sh) use these.

